# A wrapper8 source requires an int reference, not an int place.
# Step 21.7 K2, S3: the record Types is written inside Bad and launched by `Bad\Types()` over its data
# parent(Types) = Bad. Its first line declares the reference `@: p int` where Bad holds the int place p (99): the
# type is checked on that line, before the second declaration is reached and before any effect -- `Observed\after` is
# not written. The launch answers 4. The former record `call(Bad; Types\code)` still has the two positionals of
# [args, code]; the substitution of DATA is removed, and it answers 5 on this scene.
# Norm: the book #structural-call (the data is parent(C)), the roles of data and code (#data-code-roles: «in code it
# checks the type on its own line»).
Observed:
    int: before 0
    int: after 0
    int: calls 0
end: Observed
int: calls 0
fn: touch () int
    calls := calls + 1
    return: 0
Bad:
    int: p 99
    A(int: v 7)
    @: s Missing
    Types:
        @: p int
        @: s A
    end: Types
end: Bad
Main:
    Observed\before := 1
    Bad\Types()
    Observed\after := 1
    Observed\calls := calls
